  ('baseball', 'published', 'Texas A&M Baseball Wraps Fall Exhibitions, Releases Full 2027 Schedule', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — Texas A&amp;M baseball finished its fall exhibition schedule with a 13-10 win over McNeese in a 12-inning scrimmage on Oct. 16 at Olsen Field at Blue Bell Park, and the program has released its full 2027 schedule, according to Texas A&amp;M Athletics.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs-sp-04.webp" alt="Olsen Field, home of Texas A&amp;M baseball in College Station, seen from behind home plate (file photo, 2015; not from this fall&#x27;s exhibitions). Photo: Ensign beedrill / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0)"><p><em>▲ Olsen Field, home of Texas A&amp;M baseball in College Station, seen from behind home plate (file photo, 2015; not from this fall''s exhibitions). Photo: Ensign beedrill / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0)</em></p><p>Against McNeese, the Aggies had 14 hits, drew 16 walks and stole seven bases. Nico Partida and Zane Becker each had three hits, and Cole Travers hit the team''s only home run in the 10th inning. Eleven pitchers combined for 22 strikeouts, led by starter Gavin Lyons with five in two innings. A week earlier, Texas A&amp;M lost 9-5 to Rice in a 14-inning scrimmage.</p><p>The 2027 season opens with a three-game home series against Milwaukee on Feb. 19-21, the start of a nine-game homestand that also includes UIW, Purdue, Miami (Ohio) and Stephen F. Austin. The Aggies then play Louisville, Louisiana and Houston on March 5-7 at the Bruce Bolt College Classic at Daikin Park in Houston.</p><p>Southeastern Conference play begins March 19-21 at Alabama. Home conference series are scheduled against Tennessee, Oklahoma, LSU, Arkansas and Ole Miss. Texas A&amp;M also plays at Kentucky, Mississippi State, South Carolina and Texas, and the SEC Tournament is set for May 25-30 in Hoover, Alabama, the school said.</p><p>The Tennessee home series, March 25-27, and the South Carolina road series, April 29-May 1, were moved to Thursday-through-Saturday formats from their original Friday-through-Sunday dates, according to the Oct. 15 schedule release. All dates and times are subject to change, the athletics department said.</p><p>The schedule also includes home-and-home midweek series with Sam Houston, with a game in Huntsville on March 30 and a home game April 20, and with Texas State, which visits March 16 before the Aggies travel to San Marcos on March 27.</p><p>Head coach Michael Earley is entering his third season, and the team returns 15 letterwinners from last season''s NCAA Tournament team, according to the department. Earley added Barry Enright as pitching coach in June. Pitcher Clayton Freshcorn, a 19th-round pick in this summer''s MLB Draft, chose to return to Texas A&amp;M for 2027.</p><p>Speaking about Enright at an Oct. 1 media availability, Freshcorn said, "the first thing that he said is that he wants to build relationships with every single one of us and build lifelong memories, that''s who I want."</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Texas A&M baseball closed fall play with a 13-10 scrimmage win over McNeese and released a 2027 schedule that opens Feb. 19 against Milwaukee at Olsen Field at Blue Bell Park.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs-sp-04.webp', '2026-10-23T14:20:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Texas A&M baseball','Michael Earley','2027 schedule','Olsen Field at Blue Bell Park','fall ball']::text[], '• 확인할 점: The McNeese recap is dated Oct. 17 and says ''Friday night''; the Rice recap says the McNeese game was Friday, Oct. 16. I used Oct. 16.
• 확인할 점: The Sept. 8 SEC schedule release listed Tennessee March 26-28 and South Carolina April 30-May 2; the Oct. 15 release moved them to March 25-27 and April 29-May 1. The newer dates are used.
• 확인할 점: SFA is written out as Stephen F. Austin and UIW is left as the school uses it; HCU, Air Force, Prairie View A&M, Tarleton and UTSA midweek games and the Loyola Marymount series were left out to keep the story short.
• 확인할 점: Freshcorn quote: the printed quote begins with ''(But) when I had those conversations...'' — I used only the sentence portion beginning ''the first thing that he said''. Check that it reads acceptably as a partial quote.
• 확인할 점: Release refers to the last season as an NCAA Tournament team and a regional final appearance; I used only ''NCAA Tournament team''.
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Baseball Tops McNeese, 13-10, in Final Fall Tune-up (Oct. 17, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/17/baseball-tops-mcneese-13-10-in-final-fall-tune-up
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Baseball Falls to Rice in Fall Scrimmage (Oct. 9, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/10/baseball-falls-to-rice-in-fall-scrimmage
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Baseball Unveils Full 2027 Schedule (Oct. 15, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/15/baseball-unveils-full-2027-schedule
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Baseball Learns 2027 SEC Schedule (Sept. 8, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/09/08/baseball-learns-2027-sec-schedule
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Baseball Holds First Media Availability of Fall (Oct. 1, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/01/baseball-holds-first-media-availability-of-fall
• 이용 조건: Text: original writing based on facts from Texas A&M Athletics releases; quotes as printed by Texas A&M Athletics / Photo: CC BY-SA 4.0, Ensign beedrill, File:Olsen Field Home Plate View.jpg (4896x3672)
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('fashion', 'published', 'Dressing for November in the Brazos Valley: Plan for 20-Degree Daily Swings', '<p>COLLEGE STATION — November in the Brazos Valley usually means cool mornings and mild afternoons, with about 20 degrees between them. Federal climate data make a practical case for dressing in layers that can come off by lunch and go back on after dark.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs-ls-03.webp" alt="Texas A&amp;M&#x27;s Memorial Student Center, with Kyle Field behind it, seen from Simpson Drill Field (file photo, January 2022; not taken on a game day). Photo: Oldag07 / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0)"><p><em>▲ Texas A&amp;M''s Memorial Student Center, with Kyle Field behind it, seen from Simpson Drill Field (file photo, January 2022; not taken on a game day). Photo: Oldag07 / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0)</em></p><p>Climate normals from the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration''s National Centers for Environmental Information are 30-year averages for 1991 through 2020 from the weather station at Easterwood Field, College Station''s airport. They put November''s average high at 71.1 degrees and its average low at 49.8.</p><p>The month cools steadily. The normal high is 76 degrees on Nov. 1 and 66.7 degrees by Nov. 30. Normal lows fall from 54.5 degrees to 45.6 over the same weeks. December is cooler still, with an average high of 63.4 degrees and an average low of 42.8.</p><p>Rain is part of the picture. Normal November rainfall at the station is 3.31 inches. That follows October, which at 4.93 inches is the wettest month in the station''s normals.</p><p>These are long-term averages, not forecasts, and any day can be much warmer or colder. In practice, a sleeved base layer suited to a 70-degree afternoon, a light sweater or overshirt for mornings and a jacket that can be packed away cover most of the normal range. A water-resistant outer layer is worth having on rainy days.</p><p>The National Weather Service advises making the forecast part of a regular routine so cold weather does not come as a surprise. It notes that the coldest part of the day is usually early morning, and it recommends dressing in layers and covering exposed skin when real cold arrives.</p><p>Layering also matters for football fans. Texas A&amp;M''s official athletics schedule lists two November home games at Kyle Field: Tennessee on Saturday, Nov. 14, with kickoff time not yet set, and Texas on Friday, Nov. 27, at 6:30 p.m. The normal low for Nov. 27 is 46.4 degrees. Fans at the night game may want a warm layer for after sundown, along with the maroon.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Federal climate normals show College Station''s November days start near 50 degrees and warm to about 70. That spread makes layers the practical choice, including at Kyle Field.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs-ls-03.webp', '2026-10-24T09:20:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['fall fashion','weather','layering','Kyle Field','Brazos Valley']::text[], '• 확인할 점: Temperature and rainfall normals come from the NOAA NCEI 1991-2020 normals for station USW00003904 (COLLEGE STN, TX, Easterwood Field): monthly values and daily values for Nov. 1 (76.0/54.5), Nov. 27 (67.5/46.4) and Nov. 30 (66.7/45.6).
• 확인할 점: The football schedule is from 12thman.com as of Oct. 27. The Tennessee kickoff time was listed as ''Flex'', and the Nov. 27 Texas kickoff at 6:30 PM is assumed to be Central time. Kickoff times may change.
• 확인할 점: Kyle Field bag, blanket and umbrella rules could not be confirmed on the current official A-Z page (the page loads by JavaScript), so stadium-item rules are left out.
• 확인할 점: The NWS layering and ''coldest part of the day'' advice comes from its cold-weather safety pages, which are written for extreme cold. The article frames them that way.
• 확인할 점: The ''base layer / sweater / packable jacket'' paragraph is service advice that follows from the data. No brands or products are named.
• 확인할 점: Photo: the Commons page describes it as ''Texas A&M University Memorial Student Center with Kyle Field in the Background taken from Simpson Drill Field''. Check the image for prominent faces. The first choice (TAMU Kyle Field 2022-01-14 3.jpg) was replaced because sp.json already uses it.
• 원문(NOAA NCEI — U.S. Climate Normals 1991-2020, monthly, station USW00003904 College Station): https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/services/data/v1?dataset=normals-monthly-1991-2020&stations=USW00003904&format=json&dataTypes=MLY-TMAX-NORMAL,MLY-TMIN-NORMAL,MLY-TAVG-NORMAL,MLY-PRCP-NORMAL&includeStationName=true
• 원문(NOAA NCEI — U.S. Climate Normals 1991-2020, daily, station USW00003904): https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/services/data/v1?dataset=normals-daily-1991-2020&stations=USW00003904&format=csv&dataTypes=DLY-TMAX-NORMAL,DLY-TMIN-NORMAL&startDate=2010-01-01&endDate=2010-12-31
• 원문(National Weather Service — Prepare for Cold Weather): https://www.weather.gov/safety/cold-before
• 원문(National Weather Service — During Extremely Cold Weather): https://www.weather.gov/safety/cold-during
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics (12thman.com) — 2026 Football Schedule): https://12thman.com/sports/football/schedule/2026
• 이용 조건: Text: original wording based on NOAA/NWS data (U.S. federal works, public domain) and the Texas A&M Athletics schedule (facts only). / Photo: CC BY-SA 4.0, Oldag07, File:TAMU MSC Kyle Field Simpson Drill Field.jpg
• 발행: 대표님 요청으로 승인 대기 없이 바로 발행'),
  ('aggie-football', 'published', 'Texas A&M Falls 31-20 at No. 13 Alabama, Drops to 4-4 Before Bye Week', '<p>TUSCALOOSA, Ala. — Texas A&amp;M lost 31-20 to No. 13 Alabama on Saturday afternoon at Bryant-Denny Stadium after the teams went into halftime tied 17-17, according to Texas A&amp;M Athletics.</p><img src="/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs-sp-01.webp" alt="Kyle Field and the 12th Man statue at Texas A&amp;M University in College Station (file photo, 2022; not from Saturday&#x27;s game in Tuscaloosa). Photo: Oldag07 / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0)"><p><em>▲ Kyle Field and the 12th Man statue at Texas A&amp;M University in College Station (file photo, 2022; not from Saturday''s game in Tuscaloosa). Photo: Oldag07 / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0)</em></p><p>The loss drops the Aggies to 4-4 overall and 1-4 in Southeastern Conference play. Texas A&amp;M has lost three of its last four SEC games, falling at LSU and Missouri before Saturday''s setback, according to the team''s official schedule.</p><p>Alabama scored first when Dijon Lee Jr. returned an interception 39 yards on the Aggies'' opening drive. Senior quarterback Marcel Reed answered with a 9-yard touchdown pass to junior wide receiver Mario Craver, and Reed later ran 4 yards for a score that gave Texas A&amp;M a 14-10 lead in the second quarter. Kicker David Olano made field goals of 32 and 25 yards, the second putting the Aggies ahead 20-17 on their first drive of the second half.</p><p>Alabama retook the lead on the first play of the fourth quarter when Keelon Russell threw a 3-yard touchdown pass to Marshall Pritchett. Kaleb Edwards added an 8-yard touchdown catch with 10:06 to play to make it 31-20, the school said.</p><p>Reed completed 14 of 21 passes for 163 yards with one touchdown and two interceptions and ran for 23 yards and a score. Craver caught six passes for 45 yards, and freshman running back KJ Edwards ran for 43 yards on eight carries. Texas A&amp;M finished with 278 yards of offense.</p><p>On defense, senior linebacker Daymion Sanford had a season-high eight tackles, and senior cornerback Dezz Ricks intercepted a pass in Alabama territory in the second quarter, setting up a field goal. The Aggies held Alabama to 5-for-12 on third down. Olano is 13-for-13 on field goals this season; the athletics department said he is the first Texas A&amp;M kicker since at least 1986 to start a season that way.</p><p>"We have to get a lot better as a football team," head coach Mike Elko said after the game, according to remarks posted by Texas A&amp;M Athletics. Looking ahead to the final month, he added, "we''ve got to go finish November with some pride about who we represent and how we do it."</p><p>Reed said the team made plays throughout the game. "We just had to do that for all four quarters, and we didn''t quite get it done the last quarter," he said. Texas A&amp;M has a bye this week and next plays at South Carolina on Saturday, Nov. 7.</p><p><em>※ This article was written with the help of AI, based on public and official sources.</em></p>', 'Texas A&M was tied 17-17 at halftime in Tuscaloosa but gave up two fourth-quarter touchdowns in a 31-20 loss to No. 13 Alabama. The Aggies are 4-4 overall and 1-4 in SEC play.', '/sites/breakingbcs/photos/bcs-sp-01.webp', '2026-10-25T09:15:00-05:00'::timestamptz, array['Texas A&M football','Alabama','Marcel Reed','SEC','Mike Elko']::text[], '• 확인할 점: All game facts, stats and quotes are from the official 12thman.com game recap (Oct. 24, 2026) and the 12thman.com 2026 schedule page; box score was not separately cross-checked.
• 확인할 점: Quotes are taken from the postgame interview excerpts printed on the recap page; the release did not say whether they were edited. Elko quote is two separate excerpts from the same answer.
• 확인할 점: The recap does not list Alabama''s total yardage or the Aggies'' rankings; left out.
• 확인할 점: Reed''s 49 career TD passes (fourth on A&M''s all-time list) mentioned in the release was left out to keep the story short; can be added.
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — Football Drops 31-20 Battle to No. 13 Alabama (Oct. 24, 2026)): https://12thman.com/news/2026/10/24/aggies-at-alabama
• 원문(Texas A&M Athletics — 2026 Football Schedule (accessed Oct. 27, 2026)): https://12thman.com/sports/football/schedule
• 이용 조건: Text: original writing based on facts from Texas A&M Athletics releases; quotes as printed by Texas A&M Athletics / Photo: CC BY-SA 4.0, Oldag07, File:TAMU Kyle Field 2022-01-14 1.jpg (4032x3024)
